From 8b78901b3338d09bc788f189ed5793323e42069f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daurosk <354202035+daurosk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 23:28:22 -0900
Subject: [PATCH] Co-op title: Skip title screen chooses natively, presses
 nothing

oot-remake-multiplayer's patch 0028 (player report 133). Longshot's Skip
title screen (Insert menu, Gameplay; off by default) tapped A every 2 s
from 20 s after the start, so A went to whatever had the focus: a player
who wanted a new game, or co-op's Host and Join, was carried into the
newest save. The row stays; its taps go.

host/oot_autoload.c arms as before (the row on and a save on disk) and
makes the choices the game's own way: at a menu screen's update on the
game's thread (host/oot_menu.c hos_oot_menu_tick, both platforms), the
screen's one focused button, steady for 1 s, gets the game's
Button::Decide (main+0x3771db0, with 0: the call the game's screens make
for a button chosen without its own input). Only three screens, in
order, known by their vtables (host/hos_skip_title.h): the title's
Continue (Pa_Button_02), the load list's focused file, its question's
first answer (Pa_CheckButton_00). Any other screen with a focused
button, a known one out of order or focused elsewhere, stops it for
good. It also stops on any button, key or click of the player's
(hos_coop_pad), when the co-op module holds it (host/coop_bridge.c
hos_coop_title_hold_now, the module's optional hos_coop_title_hold:
hosting, joining, a session, the host's save coming), once Link runs or
after 120 s. Each choice and each stop is logged with its reason.
